f 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552461 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-6x+11$ for $x\\ge 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552461 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78fb1a6e-17a5-5dc5-a34e-f2b26dac2b07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552461 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}-6x+11 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-{3}^{2}+11 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}-9+11 \\\\  & =(x-3)^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=(x-3)^{2}+2\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=(y-3)^{2}+2\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(y-3)^{2}+2 \\\\ x-2 & =(y-3)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{x-2} & =y-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x-2}+3 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 3$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 3.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{x-2}+3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}$ for $x\\le 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b20bccf7-d7c5-5c00-be58-d20d6291b56b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552491 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =4x-{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-4x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-((x-2)^{2}-4) \\\\  & =-(x-2)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-(x-2)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx=-(y-2)^{2}+4\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y-2)^{2}+4 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4-x \\\\ y-2 & =-\\sqrt{4-x} \\\\ y & =2-\\sqrt{4-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the negative square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is $x\\le 2,$ then the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is  ${f}^{-1}\\le 2.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=2-\\sqrt{4-x}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+22x-21$ for $x\\ge 11.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0af0588-6d95-587e-b2d0-7c014fb9577c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552501 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{2}+22x-21 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-22x)-21 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 11x+{11}^{2}-{11}^{2})-21 \\\\  & =-((x-11)^{2}-121)-21 \\\\  & =-(x-11)^{2}+121-21 \\\\  & =-(x-11)^{2}+100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-(x-11)^{2}+100\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-(y-11)^{2}+100\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-(y-11)^{2}+100 \\\\ x-100 & =-(y-11)^{2} \\\\ 100-x & =(y-11)^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{100-x} & =y-11 \\\\ \\sqrt{100-x}+11 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if $x\\ge 11$ is the domain of $f,$ then the range of the inverse is ${f}^{-1}\\ge 11.$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt{100-x}+11\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552506 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186552329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552506 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175